    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2026/02/adidas-adizero-boston-13-quick.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is firm-leaning overall, with a firmer heel and a slightly softer lateral forefoot; impact protection is solid at 37/30 mm but feels more performance-firm than plush.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate with only a little forefoot bounce; rods plus rocker deliver a snappy roll-through for tempo work, but it is less springy than expected and needs about 20-30 miles to break in.",
        "Stability: Torsional/forefoot rigidity is high (not very flexible), the heel counter is stiff, and lateral heel/midfoot support is strong via rod extension and sole flare, but the platform has a medial bias that can be problematic for runners needing medial midfoot support.",
        "Durability: Outsole longevity is excellent, with tank-like Lighttraxion rubber showing essentially no wear after about 40 miles; minimal midsole breakdown suggests above-average lifespan."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/04/adidas-adizero-boston-13-review-7.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Forefoot cushioning is deeper and softer with more Lightstrike Pro, giving good impact protection and ground feel up front, while heel cushioning is still on the firmer side and only moderately forgiving.",
        "Responsiveness: The setup feels dynamic with snappy flex/toe-off from Lightstrike Pro plus Energy Rods, and it shines more at faster paces than slower, easier running.",
        "Stability: Testers describe a consistent, linear, stable ride; structured upper lockdown plus a rigid/stiff heel counter improve heel hold and lateral support.",
        "Durability: The outsole uses a dual-rubber layout (Continental + Lighttraxxion), indicating a durability-focused design, but no long-term outsole wear or material longevity results are reported in this excerpt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/adidas-adizero-boston-13-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Despite 14% more Lightstrike Pro in the forefoot, the ride remains relatively firm and close to Boston 12, with improved step-in comfort from added collar/heel/tongue padding but not a plush recovery feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The Lightstrike + Lightstrike Pro midsole with EnergyRods gives a firm, snappy, tempo-friendly ride, though reviewers still wanted more forefoot bounce/energy return.",
        "Stability: Rearfoot stability is aided by Lightstrike in the heel, and the redesigned padded heel counter plus more structured upper improve hold and lateral security, but some heel-lift/lockdown issues were reported.",
        "Durability: Expected durability is a strength, with Lightstrike Pro described as holding up well over time and the Continental + LightTraxion outsole setup built to handle high mileage and wear."
      ]
    }
